<%# One remembered create, shown in the taxonomy tree it would have joined.
    #
    # A tree node is more than a row: it is a drag target, a rename trigger, an
    # edit menu, and a details link, and every one of those needs an id. A
    # remembered create has no id (ADR 0019), so this row is the read-only half of
    # the node — the same `.taxonomy-row` shape so it reads as a member of the
    # tree, with none of the controls that would have nowhere to go.
    #
    # It is deliberately **not** `.taxonomy-node`: `taxonomy_tree_controller` counts
    # `.taxonomy-node` children to place insert separators and to compute a new
    # sibling's position, and a row that is in neither list cannot be dragged,
    # moved past, or renamed by a reader who cannot see it yet. It sits after the
    # real roots, because a remembered create has no parent to hang it under — the
    # same accepted limit the drafts page has for a create's story or scene.
    #
    # The name comes from `draft_pending_record_label` rather than `record.name`
    # because a remembered create is not validated: a taxonomy create with no name
    # has no name to print, and the row would carry a badge and nothing to hang it
    # on. It is titled by the type it would create instead. %>
<li class="taxonomy-pending">
  <div class="taxonomy-row d-flex align-items-center gap-2 border-bottom">
    <span class="taxonomy-name-area d-flex align-items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
      <span class="taxonomy-name-text text-break">
        <span class="entity-title"><%= draft_pending_record_label(record) %></span>
        <%= render "shared/draft_pending_badge", state: draft_pending_state(record) %>
        <% if record.description.present? %>
          <span class="entity-description d-block"><%= record.description %></span>
        <% end %>
      </span>
    </span>
  </div>
</li>